[size=3][u][b]Save state[/b][/u][/size]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[size=3][u][b]Usage[/b][/u][/size]

Open the map and click the [b]Wares on Visible Stations[/b] tab in the Object List panel tab strip. The tab is visible whenever you are on any map view.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-VisibleWareOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/visible_ware_overview_tab.png[/img]

All wares present at stations currently visible on the map are listed, grouped by transport type.

[size=3][u][i]Ware row[/i][/u][/size]

Each ware row contains:
[list]
[*] [b]+/-[/b] expand button on the left to reveal per-station detail.
[*] Ware icon and name.
[*] Total production per hour (shown in green).
[*] Total consumption per hour (shown in red).
[*] Total stock across all visible stations handling this ware.
[*] Number of visible stations handling this ware.
[/list]
[size=3][u][i]Station sub-row[/i][/u][/size]

Click [b]+[/b] on a ware row to expand it. Each station that handles the ware gets a sub-row:
[list]
[*] Station name with sector shown below it.
[*] Per-station production per hour (green) and consumption per hour (red).
[*] Current stock at that station.
[*] [b]Logical Station Overview[/b] button to open the station inventory and build plan.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-VisibleWareOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/visible_ware_overview_stations.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Column headers and expand/collapse all[/i][/u][/size]

The [b]+/-[/b] button in the column header row expands or collapses all ware rows simultaneously.

[size=3][u][i]Visible sectors[/i][/u][/size]

The header above the list names what is counted:
[list]
[*] [b]Sector:[/b] with a sector name - all counted stations are in that sector: the one under the camera, or the sector selected on the map.
[*] [b]Visible sectors[/b] with their number, and [b]Stations:[/b] with the station count - the stations come from several sectors.
[/list]
With a sector selected (click the background of a sector on the map), the tab counts only that sector's known stations, whatever the zoom. Without one, it counts the stations the game draws on the map; at a wide zoom these are only a few of them.

The option [b]Show all stations of the visible sectors[/b] counts every known station of the sectors shown on the map instead. A sector counts when at least half of it is on the screen; when none is, the one covering most of the screen counts. With more known stations than the limit set in the options, a notice replaces the list until you zoom in; 0 removes the limit. Several hundred stations slow the game down at every refresh of the list.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-VisibleWareOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/visible_sectors.png[/img]

[size=3][u][i]Extension options[/i][/u][/size]

[b]Options Menu > Extension options > Wares on Visible Stations[/b]:
[list]
[*] [b]Show all stations of the visible sectors[/b] (off by default): counts every known station of the sectors shown on the map, see [b]Visible sectors[/b] above.
[*] [b]Data refresh interval[/b] (1-10, default 3): Number of UI ticks between data refreshes. Lower values keep ware data more up to date; higher values reduce CPU usage.
[*] [b]Visible sectors: maximum number of stations to list[/b] (0-2000, default 150, 0 = no limit): with the option above, more known stations than this show a notice instead of the list.
[*] [b]Debug level[/b]: Sets the verbosity of debug logging (None / Debug / Trace). Intended for troubleshooting.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-VisibleWareOverview/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img]

